        917
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "α-contract verbs: α + -ειν/-εσθαι\nActive infinitive in -ᾶν, e.g. τιμᾶν, ‘to honour’*\nMiddle infinitive in -ᾶσθαι, e.g. θε-ᾶσθαι, ‘to watch’\n*Rules of contraction would suggest the ending of τιμᾶν should be τιμᾶν; but the -ειν infinitive\nending was originally -εν, and the form τιμᾶν reflects this lack of ι.",
      "lang": "mixed",
